nixpkgs: nixos-26.05 (see flake.lock; unchanged from 0/2/0)
changes: First version of series 0.3, prompted by agenthub's NATS agent platform (bnox-bg docs/agenthub-nats-plan.md decision 14). (1) New thing-scoped option hardening.network.nats (sibling of outboundHTTPS, self-declarable in .bnox/thing.nix as nats = true). Container things that set it get: slirp4netns networking with allow_host_loopback (--network=slirp4netns:allow_host_loopback=true — podman passes --disable-host-loopback by default, and this is the only working path on podman 5.8.2 rootful: the netavark bridge cannot reach host-loopback services and pasta is rootless-only), so the host loopback is reachable at the fixed slirp gateway 10.0.2.2; IPAddressAllow 10.0.2.2 + 127.0.0.1 under the standard deny-any filter (both addresses required: the cgroup-bpf filter also sees slirp4netns's host-side relay connect to 127.0.0.1 — allowing 10.0.2.2 alone deadlocks as connect timeouts); NATS_URL=nats://10.0.2.2:4222 in the container env; an implied nats_seed slot (/var/lib/bnox/secrets/<thing>/nats_seed, an env file containing NATS_SEED=<nkey seed>, host-written at runtime, watched by the usual path unit so seed rotation restarts the thing); and slirp4netns added to podman extraPackages. host-install things that set it get the same slot plus NATS_URL=nats://127.0.0.1:4222 (host netns). (3) Fix: the standard hardening bundle's ProtectHome=true made every container-thing unit and every pipeline build unit deterministically fail on the pinned podman (5.8.2): rootful podman stats $HOME/.config/containers (root's /root/.config) and treats EACCES as fatal — "Failed to obtain podman configuration"; the bundle was only ever runtime-validated against non-podman units, so no bnox container thing had ever started. The podman-touching units (container runtime units, pipeline build units) relax to ProtectHome=read-only, which suffices (podman only needs to stat the path; a missing dir is tolerated). Verified live: podman info/run under ProtectHome=read-only succeeds, under true fails. (4) Fix: 0/2/0's port-scoped IPAddressAllow entries (":443" for container outboundHTTPS, ":443 :53" for host-install) are load-invalid on systemd 260 (260.2, the pinned nixpkgs): IPAddressAllow/Deny take address/prefix only, no ports — every outboundHTTPS container and every host-install thing would fail to start the moment those lists were exercised (latent: none ever had). outboundHTTPS and host-install now allow "any" — honest degradation, since an egress-allowing filter without port scoping is no filter; loopback-only units pin per-unit allowlists in host config (visible overrides). All networking facts verified live on agenthub (podman 5.8.2, systemd 260.2, nixpkgs 8623c4c) plus a full container round-trip against the locked-down broker through the generated thing unit.
